Dear colleagues,

Please review the UAE legal and accounting aspects of the proposed assignment=
 to me of the interests of PBK ENGINEERING INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY RIGHTS MANAG=
EMENT - FZCO (licence No. 38769) in ten US provisional patent applications, P=
PA #1=E2=80=9310, including associated priority rights.

I am PBK's sole shareholder and director and the sole inventor of these appli=
cations. PBK is named as applicant. The 51-page Memorandum and Articles are c=
urrent; your company is handling renewal of the licence before its expiry on =
10 December 2026. US attorney Michael Bartholomew has offered to finalize the=
 assignment documents and record the assignment with the USPTO.

Please address the following:

1. Authority and corporate approval.
Confirm my authority and whether I may sign separately for PBK and personally=
. Review and amend the resolution approving the related-party transaction und=
er the current Articles, and identify required approvals and evidence of auth=
ority for US counsel.

2. Chain of title.
Review the basis of PBK's rights, existing agreements and transfer restrictio=
ns. Identify any additional documents required.

3. Settlement and tax.
Please use the attached Statement of Reconciliation and Schedule A, which rec=
ord 15 payments personally funded by me, totalling USD 21,828, replacing the =
earlier total of USD 22,593. For PPA #10, the first payment attempt through t=
he first bank failed; one payment of USD 765 succeeded after another invoice =
was issued. Only one payment is included.

The total consists of USD 10,828 for PPA #1-10 and associated NDA work, USD 4=
,600 for patent searches, and USD 6,400 advanced to Ali Shalchi for preparati=
on and filing work on NPPA #1. Ali supplied a work report, but did not comple=
te that work. I confirm that the reported scope corresponds to the advance; t=
his amount is not being treated as disputed for this review. Please record it=
 as an advance for unfinished work, not as payment for a completed filing.
Please reconcile the expenses and PBK's liability to me, assess whether the v=
erified debt may be discharged through the assignment, and document the settl=
ement. Identify valuation requirements, tax implications (including corporate=
 tax and VAT), related-party requirements and creditor-protection restriction=
s.

4. Execution and licence.
Identify required signatures, certification, translations and registration st=
eps, and whether electronic signing is acceptable. Confirm the renewal timeli=
ne and provide the new licence when issued.

Requested deliverables: a short written response, an amended corporate resolu=
tion, any necessary amendments to the assignment and settlement agreement, an=
 accounting reconciliation and execution instructions.

Please confirm what is covered by our existing service arrangement, the fee f=
or additional work and the completion timeline. Additional paid services requ=
ire prior agreement. The target is a signing-ready package in the first half =
of November 2026.

Attached: PBK_Kozin_Reconciliation_21828_EN.pdf (Statement of Reconciliation =
and Schedule A). Please review and confirm or amend the reconciliation agains=
t PBK's records.

I will provide the draft assignment documents, application schedule, Michael'=
s comments and supporting payment records as needed. Please identify any furt=
her materials required beyond those already in your records.

Kind regards,
Mikhail Kozin


